Per-wrap tty access and caller-owned filesystem write scope.

The tty parts grant ioctl access only to named pty slaves. Remove those parts
when the pinned runtime provides per-wrap tty support.

The separate default-write-path part keeps only device defaults. All other
write roots come from caller policy; retain it until that guarantee is
available without the patch.

